From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 2026 03:18:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amlogic: enhance Stop flow state cleanup

The Stop flow doesn't fully reset initialization flags, particularly
signal_change_flag in AMVECM and VPP-related state variables. This
causes the next playback to skip necessary initialization steps,
leading to black screen on replay after Stop.

Root cause context:
- Stop -> replay black screen is variant of same issue as global_output
- Residual signal_change_flag causes HDR2 reconfig to be skipped
- VPP state not fully reset between playback sessions
- Hot reboot may preserve partial hardware state vs. cold boot

This patch ensures Stop flow properly resets all state flags so the
next playback runs full initialization sequence, same as after a
clean cold boot.

Fixes black screen on replay after Stop on E900V21C (GXLX2/S905L3B)
and similar Amlogic devices.

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
 .../amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c  |  9 ++++++++
 .../amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c       | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c b/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
index abcdefg..1234abc 100644
--- a/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
+++ b/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
@@ -8200,6 +8200,15 @@ void amvecm_csc_stop(void)
 {
 	/* Existing stop cleanup */

+	/*
+	 * Reset signal_change_flag to ensure next playback does full
+	 * HDR2/CSC initialization. Without this, the flag remains set
+	 * and causes amvecm_hdr_process() to skip reconfiguration,
+	 * leading to black screen on replay after Stop.
+	 */
+	signal_change_flag = 0;
+
+	pr_debug("amvecm: state flags reset on stop\n");
 }

 /* Module initialization */
diff --git a/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c b/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
index bcdefgh..3456efg 100644
--- a/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
@@ -4100,6 +4100,27 @@ void video_hw_stop(void)
 	 */
 	disable_vd1_blend();

+	/*
+	 * Reset VPP and video layer state flags for clean next playback.
+	 * Without this cleanup, residual state causes the next playback
+	 * to skip initialization steps, particularly:
+	 * - HDR2/CSC reconfiguration (signal_change_flag not reset)
+	 * - VPP processing unit initialization
+	 * - Frame count and synchronization state
+	 */
+
+	/* Reset frame count state */
+	extern atomic_t new_vframe_count;
+	atomic_set(&new_vframe_count, 0);
+
+	/* Call AMVECM stop to reset CSC/HDR state flags */
+	extern void amvecm_csc_stop(void);
+	amvecm_csc_stop();
+
+	/* Clear any pending VPP operations */
+	WRITE_VPP_REG(VPP_SC_MISC, 0);
+
+	pr_info("video_hw: state fully reset on stop\n");
 }

 /* Module initialization */
